    "full_teaching_text": "Practical Example:\r\n\r\n1- Grid of squarish cells.\r\n\r\n2- Get the center point of each cell using the \"Area\" component.\r\n\r\n3- Use these center points to construct circles.\r\n\r\n4- Give a defined radius.\r\n\r\n5- Extrude all circles in Z direction with a defined value.\r\n\r\n6- Monitor the data structure along the way.\r\n\r\n7- Use the X value of each circle's center point to feed the extrusion values.\r\n\r\n8- Use the Distance of each circle's center point from Origin to feed the extrusion values.\r\n\r\n9- Use the X value of each circle's center point to feed the radius values of each.\r\n\r\n10- Use the Distance of each circle's center point from Origin to feed the radius values of each.\r\n\r\n11- Notice that all along the way, you have been using Trees to feed other Trees!",
